    "findings": [
      "The seven formal pages and connected map/reverse index consistently cover the single Punisher trait implementation on the three actual autogun_p1 marks. The three MasterItem names, exact trait ID and restriction, binding rows, and icon path/attachment agree with the scoped receipts.",
      "Trigger, stacking, and lifecycle wording matches the implementation: same-item ranged kill with died result and impact point within 12.5 m while held; physical child capacity six includes one sentinel, leaving five effective stacks. Each valid processed event adds at most one effective stack, a cap event can refresh without adding, expiry removes the effective stacks, and switching away suppresses contribution without pausing or deleting them.",
      "The damage examples correctly use D=B×(1+q+n×p), define B before the additive damage pool, and hold downstream factors constant. The first-effect text correctly states the lethal attack is resolved before on_kill is queued and that later damage depends on the updated Buff cache; it promises neither retroactive damage nor same-update next-pellet behavior.",
      "The RAW comparison accurately separates the actual formatter map (movement_speed and time) from the RAW damage placeholder. Under the stated manager-ready and RAW-lookup conditions, the fixed localization source replaces the missing key with the quoted damage:undefined string for all tiers; the pages label this as static reconstruction, not a tested game screen, and distinguish the implemented damage percentages as a separate effect explanation.",
      "The validated 128×128 icon receipt matches the README and reverse-index attachment URL and in-game icon path. The focused source, link, and GFM checks in the scoped receipt report no new errors."
    ],
